## Story Description
Create the project skeleton that will house the FastAPI backend and React frontend alongside the existing Python pipeline. The existing src/, tests/, data/, and dashboard/ directories must not be modified. The goal is to establish the directory layout, dependency manifests, environment variable templates, and a root-level docker-compose.yml for local development so that subsequent stories have a clear home for their files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create directory: backend/ with subdirectories backend/app/, backend/app/routers/, backend/app/middleware/, backend/tests/
- Create file: backend/pyproject.toml — Python 3.11+, project name spendcube-backend, dependencies: fastapi>=0.111, uvicorn[standard]>=0.29, supabase>=2.3, python-jose[cryptography]>=3.3, python-multipart>=0.0.9, openpyxl>=3.1, pandas>=2.0, pydantic>=2.0, pyyaml>=6.0, httpx>=0.27 (for async supabase)
- Create file: backend/.env.example — SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key, SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=your-jwt-secret, SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@db.your-project.supabase.co:5432/postgres, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-..., SPENDCUBE_CONFIG_PATH=config.yaml, DRY_RUN=true, ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
- Create file: frontend/.env.example — VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key, VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
- Create directory: supabase/migrations/
- Create file: docker-compose.yml at repo root — services: backend (build context ./backend, ports 8000:8000, env_file backend/.env, volumes: ./src:/app/src:ro, ./data:/app/data:ro, ./config.yaml:/app/config.yaml:ro), frontend (build context ./frontend, ports 5173:80)
