## Story Description
Implement the recommendations engine endpoint and the full review workstation API. The recommendations endpoint wraps the existing RecommendationEngine from src/recommendations/engine.py and persists the output JSON to the engagements table. The review endpoints expose the supplier match queue, category overrides, and audit log for the internal review workstation page.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: backend/app/routers/recommendations.py — APIRouter with prefix='/api/engagements/{engagement_id}/recommendations', tags=['recommendations']
- POST /run — verifies ownership; imports src.recommendations.engine.RecommendationEngine; runs engine with Postgres engine and engagement_id; stores wrapped JSON in engagements.recommendations_json via UPDATE; returns the parsed JSON {recommendations: [...], portfolio_summary: {...}}. If LLM dry_run is false for this engagement and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, passes dry_run=False to engine.
- GET / (root) — SELECT recommendations_json FROM engagements WHERE id=engagement_id AND owner_email=user_email; parses and returns JSON; returns 404 with message 'Recommendations not yet generated — call POST /run first' if recommendations_json IS NULL
- Create file: backend/app/routers/review.py — APIRouter with prefix='/api/engagements/{engagement_id}/review', tags=['review']
- GET /supplier-queue — SELECT from supplier_match_log WHERE engagement_id=? AND review_status='PENDING' ORDER BY confidence ASC; parses evidence JSON field; returns list
- POST /supplier/{match_id}/approve — UPDATE supplier_match_log SET review_status='APPROVED' WHERE id=match_id AND engagement_id=?; INSERT audit_log row (table_name='supplier_match_log', field_name='review_status', old_value='PENDING', new_value='APPROVED', changed_by=user_email); returns {status: 'approved'}
- POST /supplier/{match_id}/reject — same pattern as approve but new_value='REJECTED'
- POST /supplier/{match_id}/override — body: {canonical_supplier_id: str, canonical_name: str}; UPDATE supplier_match_log SET canonical_supplier_id=?, review_status='OVERRIDDEN'; UPDATE transactions SET canonical_supplier_id=?, canonical_supplier_name=? WHERE engagement_id=? AND raw_supplier_name=(SELECT raw_supplier_name FROM supplier_match_log WHERE id=match_id); INSERT audit_log row
- GET /category-queue — SELECT transaction_id, raw_supplier_name, raw_line_description, base_amount, category_l1, category_l2, category_l3, category_confidence FROM transactions WHERE engagement_id=? AND category_confidence < 0.60 ORDER BY ABS(base_amount) DESC LIMIT 100; returns list
- POST /category-override — body: {canonical_supplier_id?, gl_account?, override_l1, override_l2, override_l3, unspsc_code?, reason}; INSERT into category_overrides; INSERT audit_log row; returns created override with id
- GET /category-overrides — SELECT all from category_overrides WHERE engagement_id=?; returns list
- DELETE /category-override/{override_id} — DELETE from category_overrides WHERE id=? AND engagement_id=?; INSERT audit_log row; 404 if not found
- GET /audit-log — SELECT last 100 from audit_log WHERE engagement_id=? ORDER BY changed_at DESC; returns list
- Register both routers in backend/app/main.py
- Verify: pytest backend/tests/test_review_api.py -v — create test file covering: supplier-queue returns list, approve updates review_status, category-override POST inserts row and audit entry

