## Story Description
Implement the user-facing auth flow and the upload wizard. Login page uses Supabase Auth. The engagement list and new-engagement form are the landing pages after login. The upload wizard is a 3-step component: drop file → map columns → watch pipeline progress with polling. This is the client's first end-to-end interaction with the application.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: frontend/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.tsx — email + password inputs (shadcn Input), Sign In button (shadcn Button), calls useAuth().signIn(), shows spinner during loading, shows error toast (sonner toast.error) on failure, redirects to /engagements on success
- Create file: frontend/src/pages/engagements/EngagementListPage.tsx — uses useQuery(['engagements'], () => api.get('/api/engagements').then(r=>r.data)); renders each engagement as a shadcn Card grid showing client_name, engagement_title, formatted created_at; 'Open' button navigates to /engagements/:id/overview; 'New Engagement' button navigates to /engagements/new; skeleton cards while loading; empty state message if array empty
- Create file: frontend/src/pages/engagements/NewEngagementPage.tsx — form with: Client Name (required text input), Engagement Title (required text input, default 'Procurement Spend Diagnostic'), Currency Label (text input, default 'AUD'), LLM Dry Run toggle (shadcn Switch, default on, with helper text 'Disable only when Anthropic API key is configured on the server'). Submit calls POST /api/engagements, navigates to /engagements/:id/upload on 201 response, shows error toast on failure.
- Create file: frontend/src/hooks/useIngestion.ts — manages state: {step: 1|2|3, jobId, columns, fileInfo, columnMapping, jobStatus}. Functions: uploadFile(file: File) -> calls POST .../upload, updates state with job_id and columns; runPipeline(mapping) -> calls POST .../run; startPolling(jobId) -> polls GET .../status/{jobId} every 3 seconds using setInterval; stopPolling() -> clears interval. Returns all state + functions.
- Create file: frontend/src/pages/ingest/UploadPage.tsx — 3-step wizard:
-   Step 1: react-dropzone accepting .csv .xlsx; shows file name + estimated row count after drop; progress bar during upload API call; 'Continue' button (disabled until file uploaded successfully)
-   Step 2: Table showing 8 canonical fields (Supplier Name, Supplier ID, Invoice Number, Invoice Date, Amount, Currency, GL Code, Cost Centre) each with a Select dropdown populated by detected columns from step 1; auto-selects if column name contains the canonical field keyword (case-insensitive); 'Start Processing' button calls useIngestion.runPipeline() with the mapping
-   Step 3: 4-step progress list (Ingesting Data, Harmonising Suppliers, Categorising Spend, Building Analytics Cube) with status icons: grey circle (pending), spinning (active stage), green checkmark (done), red X (failed). Polls via useIngestion.startPolling(). On status=done: shows green success banner 'Data processed successfully' + 'View Dashboard' button linking to /engagements/:id/overview. On status=failed: shows red error banner with error_message + 'Try Again' button.
- Verify: npm run build succeeds with zero TypeScript errors after adding these files

